soc: qcom: ubwc: use HBB 15 on LPDDR4X SM8250 when SMEM has no HBB field

Holodor (2026-10-01). sm8250_data hardcodes highest_bank_bit = 16 (LPDDR5) with a
"TODO: highest_bank_bit = 15 for LP_DDR4". SM8250 shipped with both LPDDR4X and LPDDR5,
and the upstream "Get HBB from SMEM" change only helps when the bootloader writes the
newer DDR-info record that carries an HBB field (v4+); otherwise it keeps 16. Older records
still carry the DDR device type, so: record it in smem_dramc (all record versions), expose
qcom_smem_dram_is_lpddr4() + a debugfs "ddr_type" file, give qcom_ubwc_cfg_data an optional
highest_bank_bit_lpddr4, set it to 15 for sm8250, and use it when SMEM has no HBB and
reports LPDDR4/LPDDR4X.

Why: on the Retroid Pocket 5 (SM8250), any DXVK game (Proton -> Turnip, UBWC surfaces)
hard-froze the whole SoC ~20-30 s in (5/5), silently; TU_DEBUG=noubwc ran 30+ min clean.
A wrong HBB puts GPU UBWC accesses on the wrong DDR bank interleave. Upstream candidate.

